DESCRIPTION:World Diabetes Day falls on November 14\, the birthday of Frede
 rick Banting\, who shared the 1923 Nobel Prize for the work that produced 
 insulin. It is one of the few observances with a complete paper trail: the
  International Diabetes Federation began marking the date in 1991\, and th
 e United Nations General Assembly designated it a United Nations Day by re
 solution in December 2006. The campaign exists because the disease keeps o
 utrunning the response to it.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/world
 -diabetes-day/
